# Everything a `develop` machine installs through the system package manager,
# in one unit: the distribution's build baseline, the language toolchains,
# TeX, Emacs and the cross compilers.
#
# One unit because the capability never distinguished them — every registry
# entry with `develop` installed all eleven predecessors — and because a
# single zypper or apt invocation is one transaction either way. What the
# split did provide, the engine still provides per selector: exact names are
# diffed against the installed set one by one, and a failed batch is retried
# one selector at a time, so one bad name is reported as one bad name.
#
# The `# --- section ---` banners keep the predecessors' lists and their
# comments findable; `git blame` on a name still lands on the line that
# added it.
kind: packages
capabilities: develop
requires: repos
root: yes
